For a steady velocity field acceleration is the convective term \vec{a} = (\vec{v} \cdot \nabla) \vec{v}
With \vec{v} = -x \hat{i} + 2y \hat{j} - z \hat{k} m / s, the components give a_x = x, a_y = 4y, a_z = z, all in m / s^2
At (1, 2, 4) m this is \hat{i} + 8 \hat{j} + 4 \hat{k} m / s^2 with magnitude \sqrt{1 + 64 + 16} = 9 m / s^2 → (B)

