1070:
Apple green flame in concentrated hydrochloric acid points to \text{Ba}^{2+} among the choices
Acetate solution giving yellow chromate confirms barium as \text{BaCrO}_{4}
Canary yellow precipitate with ammonium molybdate in nitric acid confirms phosphate as \text{PO}_{4}^{3-}
Cation and anion together identify barium phosphate
Joint match is barium and phosphate, the second listed option → (B)

1073:
General alkane combustion is \text{C}_{n}\text{H}_{2n + 2} + (3n + 1) / 2\text{O}_{2} \rightarrow n\text{CO}_{2} + (n + 1)\text{H}_{2}\text{O}
Oxygen demand gives (3n + 1) / 2 = 8
Solving yields 3n + 1 = 16 and n = 5
Alkane is therefore \text{C}_{5}\text{H}_{12}
Carbon plus hydrogen count is 5 + 12 = 17 → (17)
